{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794180689,"nonce":"pl4ifb8JDey96NpWCB4m4xa8Gs4=","title":"L2 — UI pass: grids fill the width, selected states are clear","message":"## Context\nOverview cards have a fixed width of 380 (`src/ui/screen.rs:512`) and sit in a wrapping row (`screen.rs:453`), so wide windows leave a large empty area on the right. Selected chips use `style::pill_active` (`src/theme/style.rs:199`), which is just `surface` plus a shadow; in dark mode that is almost the same as the inactive `pill` (`style.rs:190`, `fill` at 0.6 alpha), so you can't tell what is selected.\n\n## Files\n- `src/ui/screen.rs:425-515` — `overview` / `overview_card`\n- `src/ui/screen.rs:534-716` — Repositories page cards (check for fixed widths)\n- `src/ui/screen.rs:242-300` — Epics header chips\n- `src/ui/screen.rs:811` — `filter_bar`\n- `src/ui/components.rs:29,100` — `top_pill`, `toggle_chip`\n- `src/theme/style.rs:190-230` — `pill`, `pill_active`, `nav_item_active`\n- `src/theme/mod.rs:63,118,144` — `Tokens`, `LIGHT`, `DARK`\n\n## Approach\n- Responsive card grid: a `components::card_grid(items, min_width, gap)` built on `iced::widget::responsive`. It computes `cols = max(1, (w + gap) / (min_width + gap))`, chunks the items into rows of `width(Fill)` cards, and pads the last row with empty `Fill` space so the cards stay aligned. Use it on Overview and on any other grid page with fixed-width cards.\n- Selected state: add an `accent_soft` token (the accent at about 15% over `panel`) to both palettes. Add `style::chip_selected`: `accent_soft` background, 1px `accent` border, `accent` text. `toggle_chip` takes a `multi: bool` and shows a leading `lu::check()` when selected in multi-select groups (the Kind chips). Unselected chips are transparent with a 1px `border` and `text_muted`.\n- Use the same treatment for the active top pill and add a 3px accent bar to `nav_item_active`, so the selected item isn't marked only by a surface change\n- Update `docs/design.md` theme rules with the selected-state rule\n\n## Out of scope\n- Theme mode changes (L3)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- At 1280px and at 2560px window width, Overview cards fill the row with no empty band on the right\n- Unit test in `src/theme/mod.rs`: in both `LIGHT` and `DARK`, the selected chip background (or border) has a contrast ratio of at least 3:1 against the unselected chip background (WCAG relative luminance)\n- Selected Kind chips show a check glyph\n- Gates pass","files":null}]}